Result: P2a passed 20/20 at σ = 0.36 and 20/20 at σ = 0.40 (0/20 on CRT-unmixed controls), confirming plain LLL factors N 7 to 10 bits past univariate Coppersmith's σ = 0.25 wall once samples are CRT-decoupled. P2b falsified naive non-pure generators: empirical hit ratios to the uniform (2τ)^2 = 1/16 = 0.0625 baseline (at τ = 1/8 on 1000 trials) were 0.91 for ((a^N + 1)^N) mod N, 0.93 for (N // c)^2 mod N, and 0.83 for Lucas V_N(a) mod N — all inside the [0.7, 1.4] null band.
- P(α < 1/3 heuristic): 0.4%.

