2. Kani 2^e-Gluing / Genus-2 Richelot Smooth-Isogeny Transfer over F_{l^2}
- Target T & reduction: For N = pq with p = q = 1 (mod 3) (for general N, try O(log N) small discriminants -D with (-D/N) = +1 so p, q both split in Q(sqrt(-D)) with probability 1/2 per D; tracedata_results.md:220-248), find the two inequivalent norm-N CM endomorphisms nu_+ = pi_p * pi_q and nu_- = pi_p * conj(pi_q) in O_K = Z[omega] (omega^2 + omega + 1 = 0) of E_0: y^2 = x^3 + 1.
  - Direction & cost [T <=> FACT, PROVED]: Because nu_+ * conj(nu_-) = p * pi_q^2 = (p A_q) + (p B_q) omega with gcd(A_q, B_q, q) = 1, testing the 6 unit associates u in Z[omega]^x and taking gcd(Re_omega(nu_+ conj(u nu_-)), Im_omega(nu_+ conj(u nu_-)), N) deterministically recovers p or q in O(log^2 N) bit operations (cf. factorbits_results.md:273, conn_alg.md:129). Thus T in L_N[α] gives FACT in L_N[α] with zero exponent blow-up.
- Easy regime / transfer: Polynomial-time SIDH torsion-isogeny break and Clapoti smooth-degree embedding (Castryck-Decru 2022; Robert 2023 [KNOWN]).
- Steering step & free N-structure [PROVED algebra, HEURISTIC prime density]: Unlike Frobenius pi_p (whose degree p is secret), nu_+- has PUBLIC degree N. Sample tiny norms m = c_1^2 - c_1 c_2 + c_2^2 = O~(log^2 N) (m = |mu|^2) and odd e = ceil(log_2(mN)) + O(1) until a = 2^e - mN > 0 is prime = 1 (mod 3) [HEURISTIC: Bateman-Horn, poly(log N) trials]. Cornacchia solves x_1^2 - x_1 x_2 + x_2^2 = a (alpha = x_1 + x_2 omega) in poly(log N) time without factoring. Because Z[omega] is commutative, Kani's matrix F_{nu'} = [[alpha, conj(nu')], [-nu', conj(alpha)]] (for nu' = mu * nu_+-) satisfies F_{nu'}^* F_{nu'} = 2^e I_2 directly on E_0^2 (genus g = 2, collapsing Robert's g = 8). Next pick a prime l = c * 2^{e+2} - 1 > 4mN with l = 2 (mod 3): over the known field F_{l^2} (no zero-divisors, poly(log N) root-finding), E_0 is supersingular with full 2^{e+2}-torsion rational over F_{l^2}, every endomorphism of E_0/F_{l^2} of degree < l/4 lies strictly inside Z[omega] [PROVED: quaternion norms outside Z[omega] are >= l/4 > mN], and the 1-parameter local norm torus T_e = {u_0 + v_0 omega mod 2^e : u_0^2 - u_0 v_0 + v_0^2 = mN (mod 2^e)} (|T_e| = 3 * 2^{e-1} ~ N) parametrizes smooth e-step genus-2 Richelot (2,2)-isogeny chains from E_0^2 whose codomain splits as E_0^2 (matching alpha on E_0[3]) iff the kernel comes from mu * nu_+-.
- Why repo barriers do not apply: Working over the known field F_{l^2} on fixed j = 0 curve E_0 evades factorbits PT (factorbits_results.md:303-358), nonsmooth FROB (nonsmooth_results.md:313-357), planted mod-N isogeny walks (conn_cmp.md:121-122), and genusleak's |D|^{1/2} CM bottleneck (genusleak_results.md:404-421). The additive split 2^e = a + mN evades selfred SR1/SR2 (selfred_results.md:34-53).
- Ledger & missing lemma [SPECULATIVE]: Setup costs poly(log N); brute-forcing T_e costs O~(N). Reaching L_N[α < 1/3] requires a lemma showing that the e-step composed Richelot/theta-null splitting polynomial system in the e Boolean bits of t in T_e over F_{l^2} admits sub-L_N[1/3] algebraic elimination (Gröbner/resultant decimation) or mid-walk pruning.
- Pre-registered toy test & Python result [MEASURED]:
  - Pre-registered: On 10 semiprimes N in [500, 5000] (p, q = 1 mod 3): (P1a) verify Cornacchia setup 2^e - mN and deterministic factoring from (nu_+, nu_-) in 10/10 cases; (P1b) test whether half-depth prefixes k = floor(e/2) carry any torsion-automorphism or shortest-Z[omega]-coset-lift bias separating mu * nu_+ from fake isotropic kernels.
  - Result: P1a passed 10/10. P1b falsified local prefix pruning: T_1(Z/2^k) acts transitively on T_k, and at k = floor(e/2) the true prefix's shortest Z[omega]-lift norm sits at mean percentile 0.609 (min 0.203, max 1.000 — indistinguishable from noise), entering the bottom 5% only at mean depth k*/e = 0.684 in [0.58, 0.82] (where 2^{2k} >= mN). Any sub-1/3 solver must eliminate globally across the e-step Richelot system.
- P(α < 1/3 heuristic): 0.3%.

