3. Joux Tower / Galois-Pinned Multi-Cone Weil-Restriction (LP_exc^rel at Unit Rank >= 2)
- Target T & reduction: Constructive doubly-smooth algebraic relation / coset generation (suffmap E3 & Prop DLT, suffmap_results.md:439-484; navigate Prop H & Thm DLB, navigate_results.md:154-202).
  - Direction & cost [T => FACT (and modulus-generically => F_p-DL), MODEL-PROVED]: Finding pi(B) + 1 independent two-sided B-smooth relations (B = L_N[α], α < 1/3) at amortized cost <= L_N[α] gives heuristic FACT in L_N[α], and across moduli gives F_p-DL in L_p[α] (the jackpot target of equivtarget_common.md:27-28).
- Easy regime / transfer: Joux medium-prime / composite-degree pinpointing and exTNFS over a cyclic totally real subfield k of degree e >= 3 (e.g. k = Q(zeta_7)^+, e = 3, unit rank r_k = e - 1 = 2).
- Steering step & why repo barriers do not apply: resbarrier needs rank 2 or a rational side; grdeg Prop RR (grdeg_results.md:133-150) leaves relative rank m >= 3 at c = 0 (L_N[1/4]). subthird Theorem KH (subthird_results.md:25-50, 83-95, 141-144) refutes cheap generator heights (H_tilde = Omega(m x / n)), but its envelope corollary explicitly leaves multi-profile archimedean unit cancellation (LP_exc^rel) OPEN, proving survivors must scatter across many incomparable archimedean profiles. Crucially, subthird only tested k = Q (r_k = 0) and k = Q(sqrt(2)) (r_k = 1, whose unit log-space R^1 has only two opposite rays, no incomparable cones). Degree e >= 3 (r_k >= 2) is the first regime possessing a continuum S^{e-2} of incomparable logarithmic unit cones permuted by Gal(k/Q) = C_e. (Steering general N into a shared map psi: O_k -> Z/N uses either auxiliary cyclic-k selection or unramified Weil-restricted pairs.)
- Ledger & missing lemma [PROVED ledger arithmetic, SPECULATIVE existence]: At n = d/e ~ (log N)^{1/2}, m ~ (log N)^{1/4}, B = L_N[1/4] (grdeg_results.md:34-41), α < 1/3 requires constructing >= pi(B) O_k^x-inequivalent full-support candidates across S^{e-2} unit cones with log|Norm_1 * Norm_2| = o((log N)^{2/3}) and nonzero incremental parity rank modulo proper k-submodules (subthird_results.md:86-91).
- Pre-registered toy test & Python result [MEASURED]:
  - Pre-registered: On 6 random 44-bit Q(zeta_7)^+-split semiprimes at (e, n, m) = (3, 4, 3) (Z-rank 9, non-power relative basis (1, x, x^3) on LLL-linked quartics f_1, f_2 over O_k), run 12-cone tilted Minkowski LLL on K x K' and test whether full-support (all 3 O_k-coords != 0) vectors achieve sub-KH norms <= N^{1.5} or <= N^2 outside proper k-subspaces.
  - Result: Across 6 moduli, proper (< 3 coords) subspaces produced 374 vectors reaching min log|N_1 N_2|/log N = 0.000, whereas all 214 full-support m = 3 vectors had min log|N_1 N_2|/log N = 3.345 (0 hits <= N^{1.5}, 0 hits <= N^2, 0 incremental sub-KH parity rank) — falsifying naive 12-cone LLL steering at unit rank 2.
- P(α < 1/3 heuristic): 0.2%.

