Explicit Kills of Other Easy-Regime Transfers

1. BGJT / Kleinjung-Wesolowski Frobenius & NAV_inf shared-bridge descent (systeq_results.md:35-45, smoothbuild_results.md:507-534, navigate_results.md:154-180):
   - Initial-split ECM-Dickman scissors [PROVED]: Splitting a = u_0/v_0 mod N (|u_0|, |v_0| <= sqrt(N)) into B_1 = L_N[beta]-smooth primes costs L_N[1 - beta] for smoothness and L_{B_1}[1/2] = L_N[beta/2] for ECM extraction; max(1 - beta, beta/2) >= 1/3 for all beta in (0, 1) (attained at beta = 2/3). F_q[X] escapes only because Frobenius gives poly-time Cantor-Zassenhaus factoring.
   - Unimodular bridge collapse [PROVED]: Eliminating r unfactored (Z/N)^x bridges W_j across r + 1 congruences prod W_j^{c_{ij}} = t^{a_i} u_i (mod N) via Prop H binary exponents either collapses algebraically to one Bohr congruence when det(C_top) = +-1, or requires extracting Delta-th roots mod N (Rabin/RSA) when |det(C_top)| = Delta > 1.
   - ADD_n -> F_{2^k}-Zech & 2-adic log [PROVED]: F_{2^k}-Zech (2^k > N) is quasi-polynomial by KW 2022 (factorbits_results.md:140-164), but binary carries (T - 2)C(T) and char = 2 block any ring/group transfer from Z/N (smoothbuild_results.md:558). Appending the poly-time 2-adic log on (Z/2^r)^x to Schnorr's real-log lattice (siconstruct_results.md:111-120) scales covolume by 2^{r-2} while cutting interval witnesses by 2^{-r} (zero net gain).
2. MOV / Frey-Ruck pairing transfer, Joux L_Q[1/4], & GHS/Diem Weil descent over F_{p^n}:
   - Unit-conversion trap [PROVED]: Every sub-L[1/3] or Weil-descent method in char p uses a factor base of size >= p ~ sqrt(N) (linear polys over F_p or C(F_p)). Joux's L_{Q_p}[1/4] needs p ~ L_{Q_p}[1/4], forcing log Q_p ~ (log p)^4 and L_{Q_p}[1/4] = p^{Theta(1)} = N^{Theta(1)} (exponential in log N).
3. Diem plane/hypersurface index calculus lifted to Q (subthird_results.md:68):
   - Macaulay resultant inflation [PROVED]: Intersecting r - 1 degree-d hypersurfaces in P^{r-1}_Z vanishing at P_0 mod N lowers coefficient height to N^{(r-1)!/d^{r-1}}, but Res(F_1, ..., F_{r-1}, L) has degree d^{r-2} in each F_i, restoring N-exponent (r-1)(r-1)!/d and giving α = (r - 1)/(2r - 1) (1/3 at r = 2, 2/5 at r = 3, worse for r >= 4).
4. Smart-SSSA / Ruck p-adic log on higher-genus Jacobians J_C(Z/N) & mod-N^2 lifts (nonsmooth_results.md:203-258, 310):
   - Resolves nonsmooth_results.md:310's g >= 2 UNKNOWN [MODEL/PROVED]: #J_C(F_p) = 1 + c_1 + ... + c_g (mod p). At g = 1, |c_1| <= 2 sqrt(p) < p concentrates near 0, giving Pr[p | #E(F_p)] ~ p^{-1/2} = N^{-1/4}. For g >= 2, |c_g| <= C(2g, g) p^{g/2} >= 6p wraps mod p, dropping Pr[p | #J_C(F_p)] to Theta(1/p) = N^{-1/2} (strictly worse than g = 1). On (Z/N^2)^x, x -> x^N mod p^2 projects onto Teichmuller mu_{p-1}(Z_p), wiping out 1 + p Z/p^2 Z.
5. Semaev summation on E(Z/N) & planted Phi_2 roots (conn_cmp.md:121):
   - Semaev S_{r+1} = 0 (mod N) needs |x_i| >= N^{1/r} with degree 2^{r-1}, balancing at L_N[1/2]. Removing t_0 from planted Fricke Phi_2(j_0(t_0), X) = 0 (mod N) leaves t_0 T^2 + (t_0^2 + 48 t_0)T - 4096 = 0 (mod N), which is plain sqrt(t_0(t_0 + 64)) mod N (Rabin).
